# NEXORA STORE — MASTER BUILD PROMPT

## ROLE AND OBJECTIVE

Act as a principal software architect, senior full-stack engineer, senior UI/UX designer, cybersecurity engineer, and product strategist.

Design, build, test, and document **Nexora Store**, a premium, cross-platform digital software application marketplace.

Nexora Store enables users to discover software, explore product details, select a supported operating system, purchase software licenses, download authorized installers, and manage purchased applications.

The supported platforms are:

- macOS — DMG, PKG, and other verified distribution formats.
- Windows — EXE, MSI, and other verified distribution formats.
- Linux — AppImage, DEB, RPM, and other verified distribution formats.
- Android — APK downloads or official Google Play listings.

The store must display only verified, genuinely available builds for each application. Do not assume that every application supports all four operating systems.

This is an application store, NOT a general shopping marketplace. Do not design it like Amazon, Flipkart, or a conventional retail catalog.

The final product should feel like a sophisticated, trustworthy software ecosystem with an editorial discovery experience, excellent typography, polished interactions, and a professional account dashboard.

Build a working full-stack application, not merely a static mockup.

