# 6. CROSS-PLATFORM APPLICATION DETAILS

This is one of Nexora Store's most important features.

Every application has a dedicated details page and a platform selector.

An application may have different installers, versions, architectures, licensing terms, and system requirements for different platforms.

Never assume that one application automatically exists on macOS, Windows, Linux, and Android.

## Platform selector

Build polished, selectable platform cards for:

- macOS.
- Windows.
- Linux.
- Android.

Display a platform only when a valid, verified build or supported official distribution route exists.

Unsupported platforms must show a clear unavailable state rather than an invalid download button.

## macOS compatibility

Where supported, distinguish:

- Intel x86_64.
- Apple Silicon ARM64.
- Universal binaries.

Show minimum supported macOS version and other verified requirements.

Support formats such as DMG and PKG where applicable.

## Windows compatibility

Show verified architecture and requirements, including x64 or ARM64 where supported.

Support formats such as EXE and MSI.

## Linux compatibility

Show supported distributions, architectures, dependencies, and package types when known.

Support formats such as AppImage, DEB, and RPM where available.

## Android compatibility

Show verified Android minimum version, architecture or package compatibility where applicable, application version, and file size.

Use APK distribution only when the publisher authorizes it. Otherwise, link to the official Google Play listing.

Clearly warn users when installing packages outside official app stores and provide appropriate publisher and integrity information.

## Download panel

After platform selection, display:

- Selected platform.
- Architecture.
- Version.
- Installer format.
- File size.
- Release date.
- Minimum system requirements.
- License requirements.
- Publisher.
- SHA-256 checksum, when available.
- Digital signature or authenticity information, when available.
- Download or purchase action.

For paid applications, show the purchase CTA until the user has a verified entitlement.

After successful purchase verification, show the authorized download action.

Clearly distinguish:
- Direct installer download.
- External official download.
- Developer-managed installer.
- License-key delivery.
- Subscription activation.

Never invent download links, package files, compatibility claims, or checksums.

